{"id": "EUVD-2026-81753", "enisaUuid": "96ef40fc-080d-36f7-8c52-5501f64f2e81", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlwt_bpf: Restore reserved headroom after xmit program\n\nip_finish_output2() expands an skb to LL_RESERVED_SPACE(dev) before LWT\nxmit. An LWT_XMIT BPF program can then modify the skb head and still\nreturn BPF_OK, so bpf_xmit() rechecks the remaining headroom before the\nskb continues to neighbour output.\n\nThat recheck uses dst->dev->hard_header_len. This is not enough for the\nneighbour cached-header path: neigh_hh_output() copies the cached hardware\nheader using the aligned hh_cache size, HH_DATA_MOD for short headers or\nHH_DATA_ALIGN(hh_len) otherwise.\n\nOn Ethernet, hard_header_len is 14 but the cached copy needs 16 bytes. If\nan LWT_XMIT BPF program calls bpf_skb_change_head(skb, 1, 0), the skb can\nstill have 15 bytes of headroom after the program. The existing check\naccepts that, after which neigh_hh_output() hits its headroom warning and\ndrops the skb.\n\nUse LL_RESERVED_SPACE(dst->dev) in the post-BPF headroom check to match\nthe reservation made before LWT xmit.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:58:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/753e5cdcca5474d230d62bb3489e5168ab27c272", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c488071c3441fa34f5a87cd6c12ce2cc6304f20e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a38c0eb447e2dd0120a2ebcdba470f9505ac8907", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de2b2004e16f2930eb689175e2c1998b0a68d499", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d043e24520a273c362be5dd7d9c82796879a49b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7cf561843ed0ad57501892a65abb77957e6c800f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/179a5b2171573d94a25c9aa8e1c9f9ac352ad316", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fe7007aed9ad069b2bd77e5d0c875c64f5c0269"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p997-jc38-xxh3", "CVE-2026-90160"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07e95654-5ba8-3202-8023-a35353d4f7df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "15e4708d-b98c-37e5-b15e-05e912a163fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "1d42221c-c6f5-3cc0-a938-6454f6d9b35b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "33b61d57-e110-3e9d-ad81-efb9794e5596", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a0af8fd61f90920f6fa04e4f1e9a6a73c1b4fd2 <de2b2004e16f2930eb689175e2c1998b0a68d499"}, {"id": "347f9c96-af9c-309f-941b-c8582f991833", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "3937cbd5-1219-3079-90e6-c2b45f93b1db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "434aa059-e981-31ce-98e5-a09948e394c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "442ec655-a4e5-340c-af8f-878acf63f5f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a0af8fd61f90920f6fa04e4f1e9a6a73c1b4fd2 <753e5cdcca5474d230d62bb3489e5168ab27c272"}, {"id": "5d0ec78d-2bbe-39f2-9cf5-c26df13927f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "66e4cf49-d783-398c-89a0-e280a1be66f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a0af8fd61f90920f6fa04e4f1e9a6a73c1b4fd2 <7cf561843ed0ad57501892a65abb77957e6c800f"}, {"id": "8c1c849b-a8f4-34f7-aad7-94046c8a370e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a0af8fd61f90920f6fa04e4f1e9a6a73c1b4fd2 <a38c0eb447e2dd0120a2ebcdba470f9505ac8907"}, {"id": "959a56d0-001e-3352-b74c-c58e2f433277", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a0af8fd61f90920f6fa04e4f1e9a6